SCOPE NOTE — DATASETS ARE NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE

The MIT licence above covers the kgrepair toolkit's own SOURCE CODE and
documentation. It does not grant or restrict any right in the knowledge-graph
DATA the toolkit reads or that is committed under `fixtures/`, `data/` or
`eval/`, which derives from third-party sources under their own separate terms:

  * Wikidata  — CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
                https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
  * DBpedia   — CC BY-SA 3.0, whose share-alike condition propagates into
                derived material
                https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
  * YAGO 4.5  — CC BY-SA 3.0, with the same share-alike propagation
                https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
                Stated at https://yago-knowledge.org/downloads/yago-4-5 as
                "Data YAGO 4.5 licensed under a Creative Commons
                Attribution-ShareAlike by the YAGO team of Telecom Paris".
                The CC BY 4.0 notice in that page's footer covers the YAGO
                website, and the CC BY notice covers the YAGO generator
                source code; neither covers the knowledge-base data.

Anyone redistributing a repaired knowledge graph produced with this toolkit is
responsible for complying with the terms of the source dataset it derives from.
Per-source licence metadata on released bundles is tracked as a separate
deliverable.
